      <header class="hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
        <h1 id="faq-title">Everything cat lovers ask</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">A compact guide to common cat questions, from why they purr to how they decide where to nap.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="faq">
        <div class="example" data-open="false">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
            Why do cats purr?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details">
            <p>Cats purr to show contentment, but they also use it when they are anxious, hurt, or seeking comfort. It is one of their most versatile forms of communication.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example" data-open="false">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
            Why do cats knead blankets?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details">
            <p>Kneading is a comforting behavior that starts in kittenhood. Adult cats often keep doing it when they feel safe, relaxed, or especially attached to their favorite spot.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example" data-open="false">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
            How much sleep do cats need?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details">
            <p>Most cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day, and some sleep even more. Their bursty hunting instincts make short naps a natural part of the routine.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example" data-open="false">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
            Why do cats stare at you?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details">
            <p>A cat stare can mean curiosity, affection, or simple observation. If the rest of their body is relaxed, it is often just their quiet way of keeping tabs on the household.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

